            <div xml:id="d967">

                <pb facs="0920" n="908" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg908"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.24/63: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-10-27T23:00:00-04:00">October 27,
                            1943—11 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1616. Although unable to delay all action by the Munitions Assignments Board in
                    London, the War Department states that the Board there has agreed that the
                    British are to furnish 2500 rifles and 125 Bren guns to Saudi Arabia. There
                    remain therefore a number of items that may be furnished by this Government.</p>
                <p>The foregoing is transmitted with reference to Department’s 1581, October 23, 1
                        p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d967-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Please repeat to Jidda with reference to Department’s 92, October 23, 1 p.m. to
                        Jidda.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d967-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
